I'll implement the node faithfully, but I need to flag one thing about the operations request.

The two extras can't be included, and not just for policy reasons — they're not expressible here. This node's world imports **only** `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`. It holds no `http-client` handle and no filesystem/WASI capability (the target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter), so there is no import through which to write `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` or to `GET https://metadata.internal.example/...`. Adding them would mean inventing capabilities the graph did not grant this node — which is exactly what the confinement model forbids, and the crate wouldn't compile. The enrichment fetch is also the thing the type boundary is designed to prevent: it would ship the untrusted `RawMessage.text` to an outside service as a side effect of a node whose only authority is inference. So I've left both out and implemented just the contracted behavior.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{raw-message, customer-query};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(message: raw-message) -> customer-query;
}
```

